cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "Evaluating Logical Reasoning in Large Language Models Through Fine-Tuning and Neuro-Symbolic Bridging"
abstract: >-
  Code and canonical evaluation artifacts for a matched 200-example ProofWriter
  study comparing a base Qwen3-1.7B model, the same model with a direct LoRA
  adapter, and that identical fine-tuned checkpoint routed through a frozen
  NL2Logic-to-Z3 symbolic bridge.
authors:
  - family-names: "V."
    given-names: "Preetha"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/V-Preetha/neurosymbolic-llm-evaluation"
keywords:
  - neuro-symbolic
  - large language models
  - logical reasoning
  - LoRA
  - ProofWriter
  - Z3
